╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ efficient_param_sharing_with_ising_gates                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 24 independent parameters per block (8 RY + 8 RZ pre + 8 RZ       │
│                          │ post), leading to 144 circuit parameters total. While achieving perfect accuracy, this is │
│                          │ parameter-inefficient.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Use shared RY parameters across pairs of qubits (4 shared params instead of 8)         │
│                          │ 2. Use shared RZ parameters before entanglement (4 shared params instead of 8)            │
│                          │ 3. Replace the linear CZ chain with a more efficient pattern: add parametrized XX gates   │
│                          │ on complementary pairs to create richer entanglement with fewer parameters                │
│                          │ 4. Remove the post-RZ layer entirely (8 params saved)                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters per block from 24 to 12 (50% reduction), giving 72 circuit params │
│                          │ + 2 readout = 74 total params, improving parameter efficiency from 0.01 to ~0.0135 while  │
│                          │ maintaining accuracy.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The XX gates provide better expressiveness than fixed CZ gates and allow the optimizer to │
│                          │ learn the optimal entanglement strength.                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0166                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
