│                          │ within each ansatz block. Instead of 8 independent RY parameters and 8 independent RZ     │
│                          │ parameters (per layer), use 2-3 shared parameters that apply to groups of qubits or all   │
│                          │ qubits uniformly. This maintains expressivity through 6 repetitions while dramatically    │
│                          │ improving parameter efficiency (from 0.01 to ~0.02).                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key changes:                                                                          │
│                          │ 1. Replace 8 independent RY gates with 2 shared RY parameters (applied to different qubit │
│                          │ subsets)                                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Replace 8 independent RZ pre-gates with 1-2 shared parameters                          │
│                          │ 3. Keep the CZ entanglement line (7 gates, 0 params)                                      │
│                          │ 4. Replace 8 independent RZ post-gates with 1-2 shared parameters                         │
│                          │ 5. This reduces per-block params from 24 to ~6-8, total from 146 to ~50-60                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach leverages the fact that we already achieve perfect accuracy, so we can      │
│                          │ trade some expressivity per block for better parameter efficiency, which is compensated   │
│                          │ by having 6 repetitions.                                                                  │
