│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduced_param_ansatz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current baseline achieves perfect accuracy (1.0) on all splits with 146 parameters    │
│                          │ (16 RY + 16 RZ_pre + 16 RZ_post + 2 readout). While performance is excellent, the         │
│                          │ parameter count is high and the scoring emphasizes PARAMETER ECONOMY.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. The model already converges very quickly (step 30) and achieves perfect accuracy       │
│                          │ 2. The current design has heavy parameter redundancy: 16 RY + 16 RZ gates per block       │
│                          │ 3. With 6 repeats, this creates 96 circuit parameters + 2 readout = 98 total (or 146 with │
│                          │ full spec)                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. The linear chain of CZ gates provides limited entanglement connectivity                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy for improvement:                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. **Reduce single-qubit rotations**: Use only RY rotations (remove RZ_pre and RZ_post    │
│                          │ layers) - this cuts parameters by 2/3 while maintaining expressiveness                    │
│                          │ 2. **Improve entanglement**: Replace linear CZ chain with a more connected pattern (ring  │
│                          │ topology or cross-connections) to improve information flow                                │
│                          │ 3. **Add parametrized two-qubit gates**: Use XX/YY/ZZ Ising interactions which are more   │
│                          │ efficient than separate single-qubit layers                                               │
│                          │ 4. **Parameter sharing**: Reuse parameters across qubits where symmetry permits           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new design:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Single layer of RY on all qubits (8 params)                                             │
│                          │ - Parametrized XX interactions on pairs for entanglement (4 params)                       │
│                          │ - Final RY layer (8 params)                                                               │
│                          │ - Total: 20 params per block × 6 repeats × 1 upload + 2 readout = 122 params (down from   │
│                          │ 146)                                                                                      │
│                          │ - Better connectivity and faster convergence                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This maintains perfect accuracy while reducing parameters by ~16%, improving parameter    │
│                          │ efficiency metric.                                                                        │
