│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_rx_global_layer                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves excellent accuracy (1.00) but uses 38 parameters with a      │
│                          │ combined score of 0.99. The best prior program (score 1.00) uses only 26 parameters by    │
│                          │ employing strategic parameter sharing and a more compact gate structure.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program has:                                                                  │
│                          │ - 6 parameters per block (ry_shared, xx_0, xx_1, xx_2, xx_3, rz_shared) = 36 circuit      │
│                          │ params + 2 readout = 38 total                                                             │
│                          │ - Depth of 18, gate count of 120                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation to "introduce a global RX layer with a single shared parameter" is     │
│                          │ counterintuitive given we want to reduce parameters. However, the insight is that adding  │
│                          │ ONE global RX parameter per block (total +6 params = 44 params) could be strategically    │
│                          │ balanced by removing one of the existing four independent XX parameters, reducing back to │
│                          │ 40 params while potentially improving expressivity through better mixing.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Actually, a better approach inspired by the best prior program's success: replace the     │
│                          │ current structure with a more economical design that uses fewer independent parameters.   │
│                          │ The best program used only 4 unique parameters (ry_even, rz_odd, zz_pair_01, zz_pair_23)  │
│                          │ by applying rotations selectively to even/odd qubits and limiting entanglement to         │
│                          │ specific pairs.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Let me propose a hybrid approach: Keep the shared RY/RZ structure but add a single global │
│                          │ RX parameter for enhanced mixing, and reduce the XX interactions from 4 independent to 2  │
│                          │ shared parameters (one for even pairs, one for odd pairs). This gives us:                 │
│                          │ - ry_shared (1 param)                                                                     │
│                          │ - rx_global (1 param) - NEW                                                               │
│                          │ - xx_even (1 param) - replaces xx_0, xx_2                                                 │
│                          │ - xx_odd (1 param) - replaces xx_1, xx_3                                                  │
│                          │ - rz_shared (1 param)                                                                     │
│                          │ Total: 5 params per block × 6 repeats × 1 upload + 2 readout = 32 params                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters from 38 to 32 while maintaining the global mixing strategy and    │
│                          │ adding RX for better rotation axis diversity.                                             │
