│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ alternate_entangler_xx_cz                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests alternating shared-parameter entanglers across repeats to     │
│                          │ inject richer two-qubit interactions. Since we cannot modify the fixed                    │
│                          │ `apply_ansatz_block` function, we need a different approach.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key insight:** We can encode the alternation pattern directly in ANSATZ_SPEC by using a │
│                          │ clever parameter-sharing strategy:                                                        │
│                          │ - Use XX gates (parametrized) for all entanglement positions                              │
│                          │ - Share parameters strategically so that the same parameter appears in both even and odd  │
│                          │ repeats                                                                                   │
│                          │ - This allows the optimizer to learn effective XX rotations that work across all repeats  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ However, a simpler and more direct approach is to:                                        │
│                          │ 1. Keep the single-qubit rotations (RY, RZ) as before                                     │
│                          │ 2. Replace the limited ZZ interactions with a full nearest-neighbor XX chain              │
│                          │ 3. Use two shared parameters (xx_even, xx_odd) to cover all pairs, matching the prior Gen │
│                          │ 1 success                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This provides:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Richer entanglement through XX gates (proven to accelerate convergence in prior         │
│                          │ generations)                                                                              │
│                          │ - Full connectivity coverage with only 4 parameters per block (ry_even, rz_odd, xx_even,  │
│                          │ xx_odd)                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Better gradient flow through more diverse two-qubit interactions                        │
│                          │ - Maintains parameter economy while improving expressiveness                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The XX gates provide more flexible entanglement than the limited ZZ pairs in the current  │
│                          │ design, potentially reducing convergence steps.                                           │
