│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_ansatz_with_parametrized_interactions                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a fixed chain of CZ gates with alternating RY and RZ rotations.   │
│                          │ While it achieves perfect accuracy, it has slower convergence (90 steps vs. 60 in the     │
│                          │ best prior) and higher gate count (186 vs. 138).                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight from the second prior program is that using **parametrized two-qubit      │
│                          │ interactions** (like ZZ gates) with **aggressive parameter sharing** dramatically reduces │
│                          │ the parameter count while maintaining accuracy. That program achieved 26 parameters with  │
│                          │ only 3 unique parameter keys per block.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed improvement:**                                                                 │
│                          │ Replace the fixed CZ chain with parametrized ZZ interactions on the same pairs, and       │
│                          │ consolidate the RY/RZ rotations to use only 2-3 shared parameters instead of 4. This:     │
│                          │ 1. Reduces gate overhead by replacing fixed CZ with parametrized ZZ (same gate count but  │
│                          │ learnable)                                                                                │
│                          │ 2. Increases parameter sharing to match the best prior's economy                          │
│                          │ 3. Should improve convergence by reducing the parameter space to optimize                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The structure will be:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Single shared RY on all qubits (1 parameter)                                            │
│                          │ - Parametrized ZZ on the chain pairs (1 parameter, shared across all pairs)               │
│                          │ - Single shared RZ on all qubits (1 parameter)                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This gives 3 parameters per block × 6 repeats + 2 readout = 20 total parameters (vs.      │
│                          │ current 26), matching the best prior's efficiency.                                        │
