╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_rz_layer_and_tune_entanglement                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of prior programs and current performance:                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Prior Gen 1 & 2 observations:**                                                         │
│                          │ - Gen 1 (baseline): 26 params, depth 24, gate_count 138, convergence_step 60 → score 1.00 │
│                          │ - Gen 2: 26 params, depth 35, gate_count 186, convergence_step 90 → score 1.00            │
│                          │ - Current: 26 params, depth 18, gate_count 90, convergence_step 300 → score 1.00          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program achieves perfect accuracy but has **3x slower convergence** (300 vs   │
│                          │ 60 steps) despite having the shallowest circuit. This suggests the ansatz lacks           │
│                          │ sufficient expressiveness early in training, even though it eventually converges.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key insight:** The current ansatz applies only RY on even qubits and RZ on odd qubits,  │
│                          │ then ZZ entanglers. This asymmetry may limit the initial parameter landscape. Gen 1 used  │
│                          │ a full RY layer, then CZ chain, then full RZ layer—providing more uniform single-qubit    │
│                          │ rotations before entanglement.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed improvement:**                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Add a final RZ layer on all qubits (like Gen 1) to provide additional phase            │
│                          │ flexibility after entanglement                                                            │
│                          │ 2. Introduce a shared RX layer on all qubits before the ZZ entanglers to increase initial │
│                          │ expressiveness                                                                            │
│                          │ 3. Keep the ZZ entanglers (which are more parameter-efficient than CZ) but ensure all     │
│                          │ qubits have rotation freedom                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Improve convergence speed (reduce convergence_step from 300 toward 60)                  │
│                          │ - Maintain or improve accuracy (already at 1.00)                                          │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count low (add only 2 new shared params: rx_shared, rz_final)            │
│                          │ - Increase depth slightly but still remain competitive                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rationale is that Gen 1's success came from having full single-qubit rotation         │
│                          │ coverage (RY + RZ on all qubits), while the current design restricts rotations to         │
│                          │ alternating qubits. By adding RX and final RZ layers, we restore expressiveness without   │
│                          │ excessive parameter growth.                                                               │
